<http://data.silknow.org/object/41650d59-9338-394d-8512-d1c6aaee9cbf>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Wrapped garment, woven in textured stripes of black, pink, orange, pale blue and gold coloured silk. The hems have wide bands of gold-wrapped thread and narrow bands with coloured designs, mainly blue and red; the borders have bands of gold-wrapped thread with stripes of chevrons on either side."@en , "Textile, striped silk wrapped garment, Sindh, ca. 1855."@en , "The complete piece would have been intended for use as a garment, clothing."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/72141934-aafb-3079-a03f-e509098accd1> ;
